    "schema_version": "1.0",
    "scoring": "layered-continuous",
    "domain": "inverter",
    "title": "D027: Three-phase three-level inverter with closed-loop current control",
    "routing": "behavior+structure+scenarios",
    "prompt": "Build a three-phase three-level neutral-point-clamped inverter using Simscape Specialized Power Systems. A split 600 V DC bus must feed a physically connected three-leg NPC power stage with clamping paths and a balanced three-phase load. Read Iref_amp from a base-workspace variable; it is the peak amplitude of the balanced three-phase current command, nominally 5 A with an operating envelope of 4 to 6 A. Closed-loop current regulation must use physically measured output current so the measured balanced 50 Hz currents track the command throughout this envelope. The closed-loop current regulation must establish promptly after startup. The measured bridge-side line voltages must remain a 50 Hz multilevel three-phase set near 1200 V peak-to-peak. Log physical Timeseries Vout and Iabc, each containing exactly the three measured phases in consistent phase order.",
